  <title><a href="https://nordicapis.com/events/platform-summit-2026/">Nordic APIs Summit 2026</a></title>
  <author>Erik Wilde</author>
  <affiliation><a href="https://www.openapis.org/">OpenAPI Initiative (OAI)</a></affiliation>
  <date short="2026-10-13">October 13, 2026</date>
  <copyright>2026 Erik Wilde</copyright>
  <presentation id="index">
    <title short="Composable Architecture for AI Systems">Composable Architecture for AI Systems: APIs, MCP, Skills, Sub-Agents, and Workflows</title>
    <toc class="abstract">AI is a powerful tool, but it is not the only tool, and most systems worth building are hybrids of AI and non-AI parts. That line between them doesn't sit neatly between domains. It runs inside every domain, and it should move as you learn. This talk looks at the mechanisms for connecting across that line: APIs, MCP, agent skills, and sub-agents, as well as at workflows as a way to move the line itself: when an agent keeps rediscovering the same business process, that process belongs in deterministic execution, not in a prompt. You'll leave knowing which mechanism belongs where, and how to keep shifting work out of AI as your system settles.</toc>
    <slide id="erik">
      <title>Erik Wilde</title>
      <img src="OAI-logo.png" title="OpenAPI Initiative" href="https://www.openapis.org/" style="float: right ; clear : both ; width : 30% ; margin : 0% 4% 4% 4% ; "/>
      <ul>
        <li>Ambassador for the <a href="https://www.openapis.org/">OpenAPI Initiative (OAI)</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.youtube.com/ErikWilde"><img src="youtube-logo.png" style=" height : 1em ; "/> <code>youtube.com/ErikWilde</code></a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/erikwilde"><img src="linkedin-logo.png" style=" height : 1em ; "/> <code>linkedin.com/in/erikwilde</code></a></li>
      </ul>
      <img src="qr-code-linkedin-erik-wilde.png" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/erikwilde" style=" height : 40% ; margin : 2% 0% 0% 10% "/>
    </slide>
    <slide id="ai-minimalism">
      <title>As Little AI As Possible</title>
      <ul>
        <li>The line between AI and deterministic code keeps moving</li>
        <li>Good architecture is what lets you move it</li>
        <li>All of it rests on foundations this talk mostly takes for granted</li>
      </ul>
    </slide>
    <slide id="llm-hammer">
      <title>A Trillion Operations for 16'968 ÷ 404?</title>
      <img src="llm-hammer.png" title="Maslow's LLM Hammer" style="float: right ; height : 72% ; margin : 0% 4% 4% 4% ; "/>
      <table style="border-collapse: collapse ; border: 2px solid #000000 ;">
        <tr>
          <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ;"></th>
          <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ;">CPU Computation</th>
          <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ;">LLM Inference</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">Elapsed time</td>
          <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">a few nanoseconds</td>
          <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">~0.1–2 seconds</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">Computation</td>
          <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">one integer division</td>
          <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">~10<sup>11</sup>–10<sup>13</sup> FLOPs</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">Energy</td>
          <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">~pJ–nJ</td>
          <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">~1–100 J</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">Correctness</td>
          <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">exact</td>
          <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">not guaranteed</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
      <ul>
        <li>CPU: One deterministic instruction</li>
        <li>LLM: Trillions of operations for probabilistic inference</li>
        <li>The LLM might still get the answer wrong</li>
      </ul>
    </slide>
    <slide id="before-ai">
      <title>Before AI</title>
      <ul>
        <li>Code runs deterministically</li>
      </ul>
      <img src="solution-composability-traditional.png" class="fullsize"/>
    </slide>
    <slide id="machine-learning">
      <title>Machine Learning (ML): 2010s</title>
      <ul>
        <li>Training models for specific problems becomes mainstream, but it is costly</li>
      </ul>
      <img src="solution-composability-machine-learning.png" class="fullsize"/>
      <ul>
        <li>One model per problem does not scale</li>
      </ul>
    </slide>
    <slide id="genai">
      <title>GenAI: 2022</title>
      <ul>
        <li>LLMs make ML more widely applicable and much cheaper, but they are isolated</li>
      </ul>
      <img src="solution-composability-genai.png" class="fullsize"/>
      <ul>
        <li>Powerful, but hard to make work in a predictable way</li>
      </ul>
    </slide>
    <slide id="prompt-engineering">
      <title>Prompt Engineering: 2023</title>
      <ul>
        <li>First attempts to better manage probabilistic LLMs</li>
      </ul>
      <img src="solution-composability-prompt-engineering.png" class="fullsize"/>
      <ul>
        <li>Better instructions, but still no eyes or hands</li>
      </ul>
    </slide>
    <slide id="function-calling">
      <title>Function Calling: June 2023</title>
      <ul>
        <li>LLMs are not just <q>a brain in a jar</q> anymore</li>
      </ul>
      <img src="solution-composability-function-calling.png" class="fullsize"/>
      <ul>
        <li>One model to rule them all is not the best approach</li>
      </ul>
    </slide>
    <slide id="subagents">
      <title>Subagents: 2024</title>
      <ul>
        <li>Decomposing problems into sub-problems for specific contexts or models</li>
      </ul>
      <img src="solution-composability-subagents.png" class="fullsize"/>
      <ul>
        <li>Models need to have a standardized way to reach out into the world</li>
      </ul>
    </slide>
    <slide id="mcp">
      <title>Model Context Protocol: November 2024</title>
      <ul>
        <li>Interact directly with context in a standardized way</li>
      </ul>
      <img src="solution-composability-mcp.png" class="fullsize"/>
      <ul>
        <li>Using tools is useful but finding the right ones is hard</li>
      </ul>
    </slide>
    <slide id="skills">
      <title>Agent Skills: October 2025</title>
      <ul>
        <li>Prepackaged mixes of prompts, local tools, and external tools</li>
      </ul>
      <img src="solution-composability-agent-skills.png" class="fullsize"/>
      <ul>
        <li>Some questions should be decided before models start their work</li>
      </ul>
    </slide>
    <slide id="decision-models">
      <title>Decision Models (RLCD): September 2026</title>
      <ul>
        <li>Move from human-friendly LLMs to machine-friendly structured output</li>
      </ul>
      <img src="solution-composability-decision-models.png" class="fullsize"/>
      <ul>
        <li>Some decisions can be followed by prescribed processes</li>
      </ul>
    </slide>
    <slide id="workflows">
      <title>Workflows</title>
      <ul>
        <li>Turn repeated processes into repeatable, reliable, reviewable, discoverable workflows</li>
      </ul>
      <img src="solution-composability-workflows.png" class="fullsize"/>
      <ul>
        <li>Once processes are stable, they can become part of the foundation</li>
      </ul>
    </slide>
    <slide id="everything-everywhere-all-at-once">
      <title>Everything Everywhere All at Once</title>
      <ul>
        <li>Expect this menagerie to change at a rapid clip</li>
      </ul>
      <img src="solution-composability-everything.png" class="fullsize"/>
    </slide>
    <slide id="integration">
      <title>Solution Architecture Is Only Part of It</title>
      <img src="ai-integration-tim-oreilly.png" href="https://www.oreilly.com/radar/integration-is-the-new-moat/" title='Tim O Reilly, "AI Integration Is the New Moat", Oct 2025' style=" max-height: 70%; height: auto; float: right; margin : 0% 4% 4% 4% ; " />
      <ul>
        <li>All of these mechanisms are about composing a solution</li>
        <li>Every one of them has to interact with APIs and data</li>
        <li>Wiring that up is where many AI efforts stall or don't scale</li>
        <li>AI integration architecture matters as much as AI solution architecture</li>
      </ul>
    </slide>
    <slide id="monday">
      <title>Monday Tasks</title>
      <ul>
        <li>Keep watching what arrives, because the line will move again</li>
        <li>Modularize by subproblem, so that you can move the line later</li>
        <li>Invest in the APIs and data that everything else has to reach</li>
      </ul>
    </slide>
